You can achieve this by wrapping your input and SVG icon in a container, positioning the icon on the right side of the input, and making it clickable. Here's a clean solution using HTML, CSS, and JavaScript:

### ✅ HTML + SVG + CSS + JS Example

```html
<div class="input-with-icon">
  <input type="text" id="searchInput" placeholder="Search..." />
  <svg 
    id="searchIcon" 
    class="search-icon" 
    xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" 
    viewBox="0 0 24 24" 
    width="20" 
    height="20" 
    fill="none" 
    stroke="currentColor" 
    stroke-width="2" 
    stroke-linecap="round" 
    stroke-linejoin="round"
    style="cursor: pointer;"
  >
    <circle cx="11" cy="11" r="8" />
    <line x1="21" y1="21" x2="16.65" y2="16.65" />
  </svg>
</div>

<script>
  document.getElementById('searchIcon').addEventListener('click', function () {
    const inputValue = document.getElementById('searchInput').value;
    if (inputValue.trim()) {
      handleSearch(inputValue);
    } else {
      alert("Please enter a search term.");
    }
  });

  // Pressing Enter in the input can also trigger the search
  document.getElementById('searchInput').addEventListener('keypress', function (e) {
    if (e.key === 'Enter') {
      const inputValue = e.target.value;
      if (inputValue.trim()) {
        handleSearch(inputValue);
      }
    }
  });

  // Define your search function
  function handleSearch(query) {
    console.log("Searching for:", query);
    // Replace with your actual logic
    // e.g. fetch data, navigate, etc.
  }
</script>

<style>
  .input-with-icon {
    position: relative;
    display: inline-block;
    width: 300px;
  }

  #searchInput {
    width: 100%;
    padding: 10px 40px 10px 12px; /* Extra padding on right for icon */
    font-size: 16px;
    border: 1px solid #ccc;
    border-radius: 6px;
    box-sizing: border-box;
  }

  .search-icon {
    position: absolute;
    top: 50%;
    right: 10px;
    transform: translateY(-50%);
    pointer-events: auto;
  }
</style>
```

---

### 🔍 Features:
- **SVG Magnifying Glass Icon** on the right side of the input.
- **Icon is clickable** — triggers a search function.
- **Input supports "Enter" key** to trigger search.
- **Responsive & clean styling**.
- Works well in any modern browser.

---

### 🛠️ Customization Tips:
- Change `width`, `padding`, or colors in CSS to match your design.
- Replace `console.log` with actual logic like `fetch()`, navigation, etc.
- You can use an external SVG or sprite if preferred.

